.Dd July 31, 2026
.Dt LOGCTL 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm logctl
.Nd validate and operate the LogCmp service
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Cm configtest
.Op Ar file
.Nm
.Cm emit
.Ar subsystem category severity message
.Nm
.Cm flush
.Nm
.Cm stats
.Nm
.Cm show
.Op Ar minimum-severity
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is the administrator and diagnostic client for
.Xr logd 8 .
It uses
.Xr liblogcmp 3
for all live operations and receives no private service endpoint or
administrative bypass.
.Pp
.Cm configtest
validates the supplied file, or
.Pa /etc/logd.conf
by default, with exactly the daemon's strict parser, including ring,
drain interval, segment size, retained-segment, severity, and rate-limit
bounds.
.Cm emit
writes and flushes one public diagnostic record.
Its severity is one of
.Cm trace , debug , info , warn , error ,
or
.Cm fatal .
.Cm flush
establishes the service's documented processing boundary, and
.Cm stats
prints accepted, malformed-rejection, client-ring-loss, provider-filtering,
and provider-rate-limit counters for the command's isolated service session.
.Cm show
prints retained records belonging to the immutable serviced identity of the
caller, optionally filtering out records below
.Ar minimum-severity .
It cannot select another identity or request an all-system view.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr liblogcmp 3 ,
.Xr logd 8 ,
.Xr serviced 8
